/-!
# The automorphism and module step for SL₃(4)

The construction module proves the normalizer lifting needed to exclude a
central L₀* image, and constructs an equivariant natural-plus-dual marking
from an internal natural summand and its graph translate. The actor in that
marking is exactly the actual K* inclusion composed with the model equivalence.

Source assembly still requires the automorphism alternatives with the genuine
Borel residual and core comparisons, and the natural-summand selection and
saturation from B.4.5 and F.9.18(4),(7). In particular neither an arbitrary
graph action nor an assumed full-module identification supplies those steps.
This module does not yet assert the completed source paragraph.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, proof of 13.8.20, printed pp.954–955
(PDF pp.971–972), combined manuscript of 1 March 2004.
-/
